    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "Hello!\r\n\r\nCould you please advice if there is a way to disable pairs for searching. For example, I search pattern `test(`. I'd like to avoid pairing in this case.",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hello!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Could you please advice if there is a way to disable pairs for searching. For example, I search pattern <code class=\"notranslate\">test(</code>. I'd like to avoid pairing in this case.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Hello!\nCould you please advice if there is a way to disable pairs for searching. For example, I search pattern test(. I'd like to avoid pairing in this case.",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
        "emojiHTML": "<div>🙏</div>",
        "id": "DIC_kwDOFoksYM4CAgqN",
        "isAnswerable": true,
        "name": "Q&A",
        "slug": "q-a",
        "updatedAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z"
    },
    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2024-07-25T09:39:41Z",
    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "With default config it should not do that, as [pairs are not created for Command mode](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/657ef75b52a548090fb7906735517b7ddbf39e88/doc/mini-pairs.txt#L118).\r\n\r\nHere is what I can suggest here:\r\n- Disable creating pairs in Command mode. This will stop adding pair for any activity inside Command line: entering command, search pattern, user input, expression to evaluate after `<C-r>=`, etc. There is no more granular pair creation: they all can be simultaneously either present or not.\r\n- Deliberately press `<C-v>` prior to the character you don't want to lead to the whole pair. I personally use this.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">With default config it should not do that, as <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/657ef75b52a548090fb7906735517b7ddbf39e88/doc/mini-pairs.txt#L118\">pairs are not created for Command mode</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Here is what I can suggest here:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Disable creating pairs in Command mode. This will stop adding pair for any activity inside Command line: entering command, search pattern, user input, expression to evaluate after <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-r&gt;=</code>, etc. There is no more granular pair creation: they all can be simultaneously either present or not.</li>\n<li>Deliberately press <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;C-v&gt;</code> prior to the character you don't want to lead to the whole pair. I personally use this.</li>\n</ul>",
            "bodyText": "With default config it should not do that, as pairs are not created for Command mode.\nHere is what I can suggest here:\n\nDisable creating pairs in Command mode. This will stop adding pair for any activity inside Command line: entering command, search pattern, user input, expression to evaluate after <C-r>=, etc. There is no more granular pair creation: they all can be simultaneously either present or not.\nDeliberately press <C-v> prior to the character you don't want to lead to the whole pair. I personally use this.",
